# Optional: your own TURN relay — takes over the built-in Open Relay default
#
# RemoteX already works across networks out of the box: it ships with
# Open Relay (Metered's public static-auth TURN, the Nextcloud Talk pattern) —
# free, no account, best effort. Copy this file only if you want a relay with
# YOUR OWN guaranteed quota instead.
#
# What you need (2 minutes, free):
#   The RemoteX agent can now do steps 1–2 automatically (window → "Set up
#   automatically — free"). This file is for manual setups, the web client,
#   and deployments that already have credentials.
#   1. Metered account → dashboard (https://dashboard.metered.ca/signup?tool=stunturn)
#      Free tier: 500 MB/month, no credit card.
#      (Cloudflare Realtime TURN is NO LONGER free by itself — $0.05/GB.)
#   2. Copy the generated TURN credentials (username + credential).
#   3. Copy this file to:
#        <agent userData>/turn.json           (e.g. %APPDATA%\remotex\turn.json)
#        web/turn.json                        (for local dev / preview)
#      or deploy turn.json next to index.html on GitHub Pages (or drop it into
#        your fork of the repo — it is git-ignored and never committed by default;
#        the Pages CI can also inject it from the TURN_URLS/TURN_USERNAME/
#        TURN_CREDENTIAL repo Secrets).
#
# turn.json schema:
#   {
#     "urls": ["turn:global.relay.metered.ca:80", "turn:global.relay.metered.ca:443", "turns:global.relay.metered.ca:443"],
#     "username": "<metered username>",
#     "credential": "<metered credential>"
#   }
#
# Media stays end-to-end encrypted (DTLS-SRTP) — the TURN relay sees only encrypted packets.
# If turn.json is missing or invalid, RemoteX falls back to Open Relay (no account needed).
{
  "urls": ["turn:global.relay.metered.ca:80", "turn:global.relay.metered.ca:443", "turns:global.relay.metered.ca:443?transport=tcp"],
  "username": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_USERNAME",
  "credential": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_CREDENTIAL"
}
